    <DataNode elementId="CATECHOL" textLabel="catechol" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="YCIMNLLNPGFGHC-UHFFFAOYSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="350" centerY="680" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, nilo-poyanco">Catechol is the &lt;i&gt;ortho&lt;/i&gt; isomer of the three isomeric |FRAME: Benzenediols benzenediols|: |FRAME: CATECHOL| (benzene-1,2-diol), |FRAME: CPD-623| (benzene-1,3-diol), and |FRAME: HYDROQUINONE| (benzene-1,4-diol). About 20,000 tonnes of catechol are produced annually as a commodity organic chemical, mainly as a precursor to pesticides, flavors, and fragrances. The anion form that is the conjugate base of catechol is called catecholate.</Comment>
